.0,0.0,0.0,-0.18286782503128052,0.0,0.0,0.0,-0.015087534673511982,-0.19537508487701416,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.03171875700354576,-0.29003262519836426,0.0,0.0,-0.8759832382202148,-3.3378546504536644e-06,-1.4305104514278355e-06,-6.735097849741578e-05,0.0,0.0,-5.960462772236497e-07,-0.6770398616790771,-0.00029273517429828644,-4.768370445162873e-07,0.0,-7.152555099310121e-07,0.0,0.0,0.0,-0.0011630444787442684,-9.536738616588991e-07],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,13079,17779,806,97295,8896,26944,1119,1378,58772,13,576,1378,58772,1030,458,6144,1372,315,26944,13,1260,6551,806,10641,825,33802,315,825,29177,315,825,26306,13,3757,1030,220,21,21,26944,2115,13,2585,1657,26944,1521,3757,13214,614,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nJohn divided his souvenir hat pins into two piles. The two piles had an equal number of pins. He gave his brother one-half of one-third of one pile. John had 66 pins left. How many pins did John originally have?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9742dfd7c82d617b228f0b445c6e8cd1c3064016cd65aa5df7eb25182b4f0ad0"},"seconds":7.972538948059082,"seed":470901818177986799,"stop":"eos","text":"Let's denote the total number of souvenir hat pins John originally had as \\( x \\). Since John divided his souvenir hat pins into two equal piles, each pile contains \\( \\frac{x}{2} \\) pins.\n\nJohn gave his brother one-half of one-third of one pile. First, we calculate one-third of one pile:\n\\[ \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{x}{2} = \\frac{x}{6} \\]\nThen, we calculate one-half of that amount:\n\\[ \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{x}{6} = \\frac{x}{12} \\]\nSo, John gave his brother \\( \\frac{x}{12} \\) pins. This means the number of pins John had left after giving some to his brother is:\n\\[ x - \\frac{x}{12} = \\frac{12x}{12} - \\frac{x}{12} = \\frac{11x}{12} \\]\nWe know that John had 66 pins left after giving some to his brother. Therefore, we can set up the equation:\n\\[ \\frac{11x}{12} = 66 \\]\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we multiply both sides of the equation by 12:\n\\[ 11x = 792 \\]\nThen, we divide both sides by 11:\n\\[ x = 72 \\]\nSo, the total number of souvenir hat pins John originally had is \\( \\boxed{72} \\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{72}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:140"}
